  "honest-alerts/src/honest_alerts/lifecycle.py:string->empty@events=vocabulary({\"alert_event\": {\"deliver\", \"read\", \"acknowledge\", \"action\", \"escalate\", \"expire\", \"fail\"}}),@<module>": "Emptying the vocabulary type-name key \"alert_event\". Same invariance as alert_state: _names reads the event members from the recognizer values and discards the type-name key, so the machine's events and every transition are identical whether the key is \"alert_event\" or \"\". No conformance case can observe the discarded name. Verified equivalent.",
  "honest-alerts/src/honest_alerts/_util.py:constant_replace \"\"\"The branch primitives honest-alerts composes from, so its source carries no `if` statement,\nternary or comprehension filter (HC-P001): a branch is a boolean key computed and a thunk looked up\nin a closed two-row table (P01).\"\"\"->\"\"@Point(row=4, column=0)-Point(row=6, column=35)": "The mutation changes only a Python docstring. The module contract does not depend on introspected documentation text, and the executable syntax is identical.",
  "honest-alerts/src/honest_alerts/boundary.py:constant_replace \"\"\"The boundary: the readers that pull from the world, the output boundaries that write, the\norchestrators that compose the pure core with I/O, and the three unit-1 doors. I/O lives here; the\npure core in pure.py takes data and returns data (P03).\"\"\"->\"\"@Point(row=0, column=0)-Point(row=2, column=58)": "The mutation changes only a Python docstring. The module contract does not depend on introspected documentation text, and the executable syntax is identical.",
  "honest-alerts/src/honest_alerts/boundary.py:constant_replace \"\"\"The emit seam into honest-observe: honest-alerts calls honest-observe's frozen emit door to\n    append one alert.* event to the event log (section 6.1, 10; honest-observe section 3). Its\n    signature is honest-observe.emit's contract exactly as frozen on main, and honest-alerts builds to\n    that contract without redefining or widening it; the return is honest-observe's own Event-or-Fault,\n    carried out as any. It is a terminus that does only the append; run_send invokes it for alert.sent\n    and run_acknowledge for alert.acknowledged. honest-observe's emit returns a Fault for a present\n    event-log table whose append is rejected, and raises only when the table is absent; this terminus\n    catches that one boundary exception here, at the I/O edge, and returns it as a server Fault by\n    value, so a failed append always travels to the orchestrator by return and never past this seam as\n    a raise (P24).\"\"\"->\"\"@Point(row=175, column=4)-Point(row=184, column=21)": "The mutation changes only a Python docstring. The module contract does not depend on introspected documentation text, and the executable syntax is identical.",
  "honest-alerts/src/honest_alerts/faults.py:constant_replace \"\"\"The single place honest-alerts assembles a fault, and the three alerts-owned table manifests.\"\"\"->\"\"@Point(row=0, column=0)-Point(row=0, column=99)": "The mutation changes only a Python docstring. The module contract does not depend on introspected documentation text, and the executable syntax is identical.",
  "honest-alerts/src/honest_alerts/faults.py:constant_replace \"\"\"Build one honest-alerts Fault record from its parts (honest-errors sections 2, 3; honest-type\n    section 13.2). code is the specific reason from the section 6b code space; message is the human\n    sentence naming what went wrong and what to do instead; category is who is responsible, a\n    FaultCategory member client or server; detail is the structured context a test reads without\n    parsing the message. It sets the reserved is_err tag true and\n    returns the Fault, carried by the return as a bare union arm, never raised and never wrapped in\n    an ok/err envelope. results is [] because alerts_fault accumulates none. Pure: reads no world.\"\"\"->\"\"@Point(row=5, column=4)-Point(row=11, column=101)": "The mutation changes only a Python docstring. The module contract does not depend on introspected documentation text, and the executable syntax is identical.",
  "honest-alerts/src/honest_alerts/faults.py:constant_replace \"\"\"Return the three alerts-owned honest-persist table manifests as data: alert_routes (section\n    5), alert_deliveries (section 6.2), alert_registered_types (section 3b), the honest-alerts twin\n    of honest-observe's event_log_schema (honest-observe section 10). Each manifest names that\n    table's columns and the indexes the module's reads need. Unlike the event log these tables are\n    not append-only: deliveries move pending -> delivered/failed and a byte-identical re-registration\n    is a no-op. Pure: the schema is fixed, so it returns the manifest as data, reads no world and\n    takes no argument. Returned as the list of the three manifests, each a\n    {table, columns, indexes, append_only} record, so a caller finds a table by its own `table`\n    field exactly as honest-observe's manifest exposes it.\"\"\"->\"\"@Point(row=68, column=4)-Point(row=76, column=61)": "The mutation changes only a Python docstring. The module contract does not depend on introspected documentation text, and the executable syntax is identical.",
  "honest-alerts/src/honest_alerts/pure.py:constant_replace \"\"\"The pure substrate: the constructors, the supervisor, the lifecycle transition and the mailbox\nprojection. Data in, data out, no world. Every column-0 function here is a declared .hd function;\nhelpers are lambdas or nested functions (the honest-observe precedent). The source carries no `if`\nstatement, ternary, or comprehension filter (HC-P001): a branch is a boolean key through _pick, and a\ntable read is the honest absent-tolerant _get, so a miss is a declared bounded case (P16), never a\nvalue filed under a hit (HC-P019) and never a bare KeyError (HC-P020).\"\"\"->\"\"@Point(row=0, column=0)-Point(row=5, column=73)": "The mutation changes only a Python docstring. The module contract does not depend on introspected documentation text, and the executable syntax is identical.",
  "honest-alerts/src/honest_alerts/__init__.py:constant_replace \"\"\"honest-alerts - the message-passing layer (unit 1): an actor model where messages pass between\nactors through three doors (send, acknowledge, register_message_type), land in a delivery queue, and\npersist until a declared termination condition is met. Mailboxes are pure projections over the\nhonest-observe event log, reached by import, never a door (honest-alerts.hd, section 1, 4.1).\n\nThe wildcard exports are send, acknowledge, register_message_type, advance, mailbox,\nis_terminated, and alert_tables_schema. Other existing bindings are available through\nexplicit named imports.\n\"\"\"->\"\"@Point(row=0, column=0)-Point(row=8, column=3)": "The mutation changes only a Python docstring. The module contract does not depend on introspected documentation text, and the executable syntax is identical.",
  "honest-alerts/src/honest_alerts/boundary.py:constant_replace \"\"\"Pull one fresh message id from the random source, a UUID v7 that is time-ordered so messages\n    sort by creation (section 3.1). run_send invokes it and applies its answer into the message under\n    construction, so the id is assigned in one place. A reader, not a pure fn, because a fresh id is a\n    read of the world: made pure it would be a hidden non-deterministic call, the leak the reader role\n    exists to surface. RFC 9562 v7 layout: the leading 48 bits are the Unix epoch in milliseconds\n    (time-ordered), the version nibble is 7, the variant bits are 0b10, and the remaining 74 bits are\n    drawn from os.urandom so two calls in the same millisecond differ.\"\"\"->\"\"@Point(row=35, column=4)-Point(row=41, column=73)": "The mutation changes only a Python docstring. The module contract does not depend on introspected documentation text, and the executable syntax is identical.",
  "honest-alerts/src/honest_alerts/boundary.py:constant_replace \"\"\"Pull the current wall-clock time as epoch seconds UTC (section 3.1, 6.1, 10). It reads the\n    clock and nothing else. A reader for the same reason new_message_id is: a clock read inside a pure\n    function is the hidden-clock leak the role declaration makes visible.\"\"\"->\"\"@Point(row=50, column=4)-Point(row=52, column=76)": "The mutation changes only a Python docstring. The module contract does not depend on introspected documentation text, and the executable syntax is identical.",
  "honest-alerts/src/honest_alerts/boundary.py:constant_replace \"\"\"Read the registered-types table for the RegisteredType record of one message_type (section\n    3b.2). It returns that type's RegisteredType, carrying the closed set of versions the registering\n    application declared, or NOTHING when the type was never registered. conn is the injected PEP 249\n    connection, held and passed. It reads the table name and columns from the alert_tables_schema\n    manifest rather than hardcoding them (section 10b). run_send invokes it (a NOTHING answer or a\n    version outside the set is a client fault build_message returns); run_register_message_type invokes\n    it to read the existing registration before deciding the re-registration rule (section 3b.3).\"\"\"->\"\"@Point(row=66, column=4)-Point(row=72, column=100)": "The mutation changes only a Python docstring. The module contract does not depend on introspected documentation text, and the executable syntax is identical.",
  "honest-alerts/src/honest_alerts/boundary.py:constant_replace \"\"\"Read the alert_routes routing table for the routes that could match a message type (section 5,\n    6.1). The read returns every AlertRoute whose message_type matches it or wildcard-matches it, which\n    the pure supervisor then filters and sorts, so the match decision lives in the pure core. conn is\n    the injected PEP 249 connection. It reads the alert_routes table name and columns from the\n    alert_tables_schema manifest rather than hardcoding them (section 10b). run_send invokes it and\n    passes the routes to supervise.\"\"\"->\"\"@Point(row=95, column=4)-Point(row=100, column=38)": "The mutation changes only a Python docstring. The module contract does not depend on introspected documentation text, and the executable syntax is identical.",
  "honest-alerts/src/honest_alerts/boundary.py:constant_replace \"\"\"Write one pending delivery record into the alert_deliveries queue table through honest-persist\n    (section 6.1). delivery is one Delivery the supervisor produced, status pending. It is a terminus:\n    it does only the write and returns honest-persist's own insert outcome; it constructs no Fault and\n    reads nothing, and it does not commit -- run_send commits once so the rows and the alert.sent\n    append share one transaction (section 6.1). It reads the table name and columns from the\n    alert_tables_schema manifest rather than hardcoding them (section 10b). run_send invokes it once\n    per delivery in the plan.\"\"\"->\"\"@Point(row=133, column=4)-Point(row=139, column=32)": "The mutation changes only a Python docstring. The module contract does not depend on introspected documentation text, and the executable syntax is identical.",
  "honest-alerts/src/honest_alerts/boundary.py:constant_replace \"\"\"Write and commit one registration. A driver refusal preserves the caller's transaction.\"\"\"->\"\"@Point(row=157, column=4)-Point(row=157, column=97)": "The mutation changes only a Python docstring. The module contract does not depend on introspected documentation text, and the executable syntax is identical.",
  "honest-alerts/src/honest_alerts/boundary.py:constant_replace \"\"\"Read and validate a registration, then persist a first registration or return a fault.\"\"\"->\"\"@Point(row=206, column=4)-Point(row=206, column=96)": "The mutation changes only a Python docstring. The module contract does not depend on introspected documentation text, and the executable syntax is identical.",
  "honest-alerts/src/honest_alerts/boundary.py:constant_replace \"\"\"Write deliveries and append alert.sent in one transaction.\"\"\"->\"\"@Point(row=236, column=4)-Point(row=236, column=68)": "The mutation changes only a Python docstring. The module contract does not depend on introspected documentation text, and the executable syntax is identical.",
  "honest-alerts/src/honest_alerts/boundary.py:constant_replace \"\"\"Run the acknowledge path, the single mutator of the acknowledgment event (section 9.1, 10). It\n    hands message_id, actor_ref, reply_payload, session and acknowledged_at to build_ack_event, the\n    pure function that assembles the alert.acknowledged payload, then emits alert.acknowledged through\n    the emit seam with the message_id as aggregate_id, so the event folds under the same aggregate as\n    the alert.sent and feeds the mailbox projection that terminates the message. It returns AckResult on\n    a clean emit, or a Fault code ack_append_failed (category server) when the append fails. It returns\n    AckResult | Fault so a failed acknowledge bubbles to the door by return.\"\"\"->\"\"@Point(row=267, column=4)-Point(row=273, column=79)": "The mutation changes only a Python docstring. The module contract does not depend on introspected documentation text, and the executable syntax is identical.",
  "honest-alerts/src/honest_alerts/boundary.py:constant_replace \"\"\"The message-type registration door: a registering application declares the closed set of\n    message_version values a message_type supports before sending any message of that type (section\n    3b.1). The world calls in here and nothing inside the module calls it; it hands its input to\n    run_register_message_type and returns what it returns. It returns RegisterResult echoing the type\n    and the versions now recorded, or a Fault, never raising. One of the three unit-1 doors.\"\"\"->\"\"@Point(row=295, column=4)-Point(row=299, column=95)": "The mutation changes only a Python docstring. The module contract does not depend on introspected documentation text, and the executable syntax is identical.",
  "honest-alerts/src/honest_alerts/boundary.py:constant_replace \"\"\"The primary send door: fire and forget with respect to the sender (section 8.1). The world calls\n    in here and nothing inside the module calls it; it hands its input to run_send and returns what\n    run_send returns. It returns SendResult (the count of deliveries queued) or a Fault, never raising,\n    because the calling link decides whether a failed send stops its chain.\"\"\"->\"\"@Point(row=305, column=4)-Point(row=308, column=78)": "The mutation changes only a Python docstring. The module contract does not depend on introspected documentation text, and the executable syntax is identical.",
  "honest-alerts/src/honest_alerts/boundary.py:constant_replace \"\"\"The acknowledge door: records that a recipient acted on a message so the message can terminate\n    (section 9.1, 10). The world calls in here and nothing inside the module calls it; it hands its\n    input to run_acknowledge and returns what it returns. It returns AckResult or a Fault, never\n    raising, for the same reason send does. One of the three unit-1 doors; there is no read_mailbox\n    door, because reading a mailbox is a pure projection reached by import (section 4.1).\"\"\"->\"\"@Point(row=314, column=4)-Point(row=318, column=92)": "The mutation changes only a Python docstring. The module contract does not depend on introspected documentation text, and the executable syntax is identical.",
  "honest-alerts/src/honest_alerts/pure.py:constant_replace \"\"\"Recognize two or more nonempty components separated by literal dots.\"\"\"->\"\"@Point(row=25, column=4)-Point(row=25, column=78)": "The mutation changes only a Python docstring. The module contract does not depend on introspected documentation text, and the executable syntax is identical.",
  "honest-alerts/src/honest_alerts/pure.py:constant_replace \"\"\"Assemble and validate one registration, apply the re-registration rule against what is stored,\n    and return the decision or a Fault (section 3b.1, 3b.3). Shape validation is a fault as data: an\n    empty message_versions set or a malformed (non-dot-namespaced or empty) message_type returns a\n    client Fault before any comparison. On a valid shape it assembles the arriving RegisteredType\n    (exactly two fields) and decides against existing: existing NOTHING -> write the arriving record;\n    existing a stored record byte-identical to the arriving whole declaration -> noop carrying the\n    stored record; existing a stored record that differs in any way -> a client Fault code\n    refused_registration whose detail names the existing declaration against the arriving one. Pure:\n    parts and the existing record in, a decision or a fault out, no world.\"\"\"->\"\"@Point(row=47, column=4)-Point(row=55, column=77)": "The mutation changes only a Python docstring. The module contract does not depend on introspected documentation text, and the executable syntax is identical.",
  "honest-alerts/src/honest_alerts/pure.py:constant_replace \"\"\"Assemble one immutable Message from its already-computed parts and validate it, returning the\n    Message or a Fault (section 3.1, 8.1, 3b.2). The impure parts (message_id, sent_at), the sender\n    and reply_required are passed in, so this is a pure constructor. registered is the RegisteredType\n    read for this message_type, or NOTHING when it was never registered. It reads the controlled\n    fields out of opts and places each into the Message. Validation is a fault as data, each failure\n    returning the section 6b code: registered NOTHING -> unregistered_message_type; no message_version\n    carried -> missing_message_version; a message_version outside registered.message_versions ->\n    message_version_not_registered; a termination whose fields do not match its condition ->\n    invalid_termination (all client). It never raises and never substitutes a default message_version;\n    the registered record is the only authority for which versions exist.\"\"\"->\"\"@Point(row=154, column=4)-Point(row=163, column=76)": "The mutation changes only a Python docstring. The module contract does not depend on introspected documentation text, and the executable syntax is identical.",
  "honest-alerts/src/honest_alerts/pure.py:constant_replace \"\"\"The supervisor: the pure core that produces the delivery plan from a message and the routing\n    table (section 6, 6.1), stateless with no memory between invocations. It keeps the routes whose\n    message_type matches the message's type (trailing-wildcard included) and whose sender_type is\n    NOTHING or equals the message sender's type, sorts the kept routes by priority ascending, and for\n    each route, for each ChannelConfig, resolves the recipient (the config's recipient_spec if set,\n    else the message recipient), computes deliver_at as sent_at plus the config's delay or immediately, and\n    builds one pending Delivery. The Deliveries in route-and-channel order are the DeliveryPlan. In\n    unit 1 the match is assumed non-empty. Pure: a message and a table in, a plan out, no world.\"\"\"->\"\"@Point(row=267, column=4)-Point(row=274, column=99)": "The mutation changes only a Python docstring. The module contract does not depend on introspected documentation text, and the executable syntax is identical.",
  "honest-alerts/src/honest_alerts/pure.py:constant_replace \"\"\"Assemble the payload of the alert.acknowledged event from its parts (section 9.1, 10, 4.1).\n    message_id is carried so the mailbox projection can match acks to their message; actor_ref is the\n    acknowledging actor placed on the payload under `actor` (never actor_id); reply_payload is carried\n    through; acknowledged_at, read at the boundary and passed in, is carried (this pure function never\n    calls now); session is the acking DOM session placed on the payload under `session` (never\n    session_id), NOTHING when the ack did not come in under a DOM session. It places no scope word on\n    the payload: the only scope vocabulary is the message's own ack_scope. Pure: parts in, payload\n    out, no world and no fault.\"\"\"->\"\"@Point(row=287, column=4)-Point(row=294, column=34)": "The mutation changes only a Python docstring. The module contract does not depend on introspected documentation text, and the executable syntax is identical.",
  "honest-alerts/src/honest_alerts/pure.py:constant_replace \"\"\"The message lifecycle state machine as a pure transition function (section 7). Given the current\n    AlertState and an AlertEvent it returns the next AlertState when the pair names a declared\n    transition, and a Fault via alerts_fault code invalid_transition (category server) when it does\n    not: a (state, event) pair the transition table does not declare, including any event from a\n    terminal state (acknowledged, actioned, expired, failed). Pure: a state and an event in, the next\n    state or a fault out, no world; the lifecycle stays declared data. The table is read by _get with\n    an invalid_transition fault as the no-match value, so an undeclared pair returns a self-describing\n    server Fault rather than a bare KeyError (HC-P020).\"\"\"->\"\"@Point(row=330, column=4)-Point(row=337, column=58)": "The mutation changes only a Python docstring. The module contract does not depend on introspected documentation text, and the executable syntax is identical.",
  "honest-alerts/src/honest_alerts/pure.py:constant_replace \"\"\"The session-scoped row of the scope_terminated dispatch (section 4.1): terminated only when\n    viewing_session is not NOTHING and some ack's acking session (payload.session) equals\n    viewing_session. viewing_session of NOTHING is the waiter view and matches no session, so a\n    session dismissal never ends a waiting send_and_wait. actor_ref is unused here, present only so\n    every row shares one signature. Pure: an event slice and the viewer in, a boolean out.\"\"\"->\"\"@Point(row=361, column=4)-Point(row=365, column=93)": "The mutation changes only a Python docstring. The module contract does not depend on introspected documentation text, and the executable syntax is identical.",
  "honest-alerts/src/honest_alerts/pure.py:constant_replace \"\"\"The actor-scoped row of the scope_terminated dispatch (section 4.1): terminated when some ack's\n    payload.actor.id equals actor_ref.id, that is, when the recipient actor acknowledged on any one of\n    its sessions. viewing_session is ignored: an actor-scoped ack terminates for every viewer, the\n    waiter included. Pure: an event slice and the actor in, a boolean out.\"\"\"->\"\"@Point(row=371, column=4)-Point(row=374, column=77)": "The mutation changes only a Python docstring. The module contract does not depend on introspected documentation text, and the executable syntax is identical.",
  "honest-alerts/src/honest_alerts/pure.py:constant_replace \"\"\"The broadcast-scoped row of the scope_terminated dispatch (section 4.1): terminated when the\n    acks slice is non-empty, that is, when any recipient acknowledged. actor_ref and viewing_session\n    are ignored: a broadcast-scoped ack by any one recipient terminates for every viewer, the waiter\n    included. Pure: an event slice in, a boolean out.\"\"\"->\"\"@Point(row=380, column=4)-Point(row=383, column=56)": "The mutation changes only a Python docstring. The module contract does not depend on introspected documentation text, and the executable syntax is identical.",
  "honest-alerts/src/honest_alerts/pure.py:constant_replace \"\"\"Compare an epoch-second integer or canonical UTC timestamp to sent_at.\"\"\"->\"\"@Point(row=421, column=4)-Point(row=421, column=80)": "The mutation changes only a Python docstring. The module contract does not depend on introspected documentation text, and the executable syntax is identical.",
  "honest-alerts/src/honest_alerts/pure.py:constant_replace \"\"\"Pack the supplied timestamp and entropy into a canonical UUID v7.\"\"\"->\"\"@Point(row=451, column=4)-Point(row=451, column=75)": "The mutation changes only a Python docstring. The module contract does not depend on introspected documentation text, and the executable syntax is identical.",
  "honest-alerts/src/honest_alerts/pure.py:constant_replace \"\"\"Decide whether one message has terminated for the viewer the read is taken for at at_time, the\n    predicate mailbox folds with (section 4.1). It reads msg.termination and branches on its condition:\n    ttl -> terminated when at_time is past sent_at + ttl_seconds; event -> terminated when an event of\n    the spec's event_type at or after sent_at matches the optional event_filter; never -> never\n    terminated; acknowledged -> it selects the alert.acknowledged slice for this message (every event\n    whose payload.message_id equals the message's id) and dispatches on the message's ack_scope through\n    the scope_terminated table (session/actor/broadcast) plus a no-match row. The no-match row is\n    reached only if ack_scope is a value the table does not carry, a program bug, so is_terminated\n    returns a server Fault via alerts_fault (code unknown_ack_scope) rather than a silent False, and\n    that Fault is the table's no-match row. It consults no lifecycle state machine. Pure: a message, an\n    event slice and the viewer in, a boolean or a Fault out, no world. The Fault travels by return.\"\"\"->\"\"@Point(row=461, column=4)-Point(row=471, column=102)": "The mutation changes only a Python docstring. The module contract does not depend on introspected documentation text, and the executable syntax is identical.",
  "honest-alerts/src/honest_alerts/pure.py:constant_replace \"\"\"An actor's mailbox as a pure projection over the events handed to it: which messages addressed\n    to this actor have not yet terminated at at_time, for the viewer the read is taken for (section\n    4.1). The caller selects the event set through an honest-observe projection and passes it as\n    events; mailbox folds over exactly those and reads nothing else. viewing_session is passed straight\n    through to is_terminated unchanged and no session is read off actor_ref. It keeps the alert.sent\n    events whose recipient matches actor_ref and whose sent_at is at or before at_time, invokes\n    is_terminated for each to drop the terminated ones, and returns the pending Messages ordered by\n    sent_at ascending. is_terminated can return a server Fault on its dispatch no-match row; that Fault\n    travels by return, so mailbox returns list<Message> | Fault and surfaces it. Pure: a fold over the\n    given events, no world.\"\"\"->\"\"@Point(row=560, column=4)-Point(row=569, column=30)": "The mutation changes only a Python docstring. The module contract does not depend on introspected documentation text, and the executable syntax is identical.",
